From b22a3d196e18b2b0e9b206a6a1921b825027dafe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:31:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 077/110] WIP: wifi: ath11k: run QCA6490 v1 as WCN6855, data
 path works

With the firmware RAM and regulatory problems out of the way the v1
part runs with the full WCN6855 parameters (op9_profile=0): its RX
descriptors and REO setup are WCN6855's, and with the QCA6390 ones
every REO error descriptor failed to parse and nothing was received.
CFR stays off to save firmware memory.

Tested: scan on 2.4/5/6 GHz, association, DHCP and HTTP on a 6 GHz
160 MHz HE network.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index 41860904b82..be9fe5c2ad7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2631,12 +2631,13 @@ static int ath11k_init_hw_params(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	 * (UMAC rings and copy engines; checked against the vendor fw-api
 	 * qca6490/v1 headers), with the rest of QCA6390's parameters.
 	 */
-	if (ab->qcom_platform && ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCA6390_HW20) {
+	if (ab->qcom_platform) {
 		ab->hw_params.regs = &wcn6855_regs;
 		ab->hw_params.fix_l1ss = false;
+		ab->hw_params.cfr_support = false;
 		/* the v1 firmware runs out of RAM on 17 vdevs; the vendor driver asks for 4 */
 		ab->hw_params.num_vdevs = 4;
-		ath11k_info(ab, "QCA6490 v1: QCA6390 parameters with the WCN6855 register map\n");
+		ath11k_info(ab, "QCA6490 v1: WCN6855 register map, v1 firmware limits\n");
 	}
 
 	ath11k_info(ab, "%s\n", ab->hw_params.name);
